 table truncation.\n35:| `wrong_unit` | `delta_source` correct but `delta_target` wrong |\n36:| `wrong_period` | the periods chosen differ from the item's |\n37:| `regressed` | compared to arm B on the same item, a previously correct answer becomes incorrect |\n48:1. the adapter emits the same prompt twice for the same item (byte equality);\n70:## 5. Revision 1.2 (2026-10-13): leak-guard canonicalization + taxonomy/receipt precision\n72:**Trigger:** Loop C WP-1 audit (`tatqa-wp1-audit-20261013`, CONDITIONAL) found: (i) the hidden-gold needle rendered `1300.0` where 1.1(b) names `1300` (latent false-negative, positive-control proven); (ii) the emitted outcome vocabulary (`wrong`) is a superset of the declared taxonomy, and `regressed` excludes refused/unknown; (iii) safety booleans are recorded as literal self-attestation rather than derived evidence; (iv) `FIXTURE_RECEIPT` has no integrity pin and its canonical path needs stating; (v) `target_unit` is absent from all 60 frozen candidates (identity conversions only) and `gold_delta_source_unit` is a naming trap - both to be resolved at prereg/item-freeze.\n76:(a) **Chosen form.** The answer-value needle is the canonical plain-decimal form of `delta_source` and `delta_target`: no trailing zeros, no exponent (for example `60`, `-55`, `1.3`, `3`, `1300`). Where the exact `str(value)` render differs (for example `1300.0`), BOTH forms are searched.\n77:(b) **Positive control (mandatory).** The check must include a self-test that injects each needle into a synthetic projection and asserts the guard fires; a guard that cannot catch its own injected leak fails the obligation. At minimum cover the `1300`/`1300.0` pair and one negative value.\n78:(c) **Coverage.** The byte-determinism obligation applies to EVERY fixture and ALL four arms (B/E/C/S), not one item and one arm.\n79:(d) **Outcome vocabulary (eight classes).** `correct`, `correct_other_form`, `wrong_unit`, `wrong_period`, `wrong` (answered and parseable, neither correct nor a specific wrong_* class), `regressed`, `refused`, `unknown`. `regressed` is assigned by the B-vs-arm comparison when a B-correct outcome becomes non-correct other than `refused`/`unknown`; refusals and unknowns remain first-class.\n80:(e) **Receipts.** Every safety boolean is either derived from executed behaviour or explicitly labelled `attested: true`; `scoring_inputs_all_synthetic` must be derived. `WP1_RECEIPT.artifact_hashes` must include the `FIXTURE_RECEIPT` hash. The canonical `FIXTURE_RECEIPT` path is `data/research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/FIXTURE_RECEIPT.json`; the copy under `research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/` is a byte-identical mirror for tracking.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,150p' docs/research/WP0_TATQA_ADAPTER_CHECKER_CONTRACT_v1.md; printf '\\\\n--- implementation contract ---\\\\n'; sed -n '1,320p' research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/implementation_contract.md; printf '\\\\n--- checker ---\\\\n'; sed -n '1,360p' research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/checker.py; printf '\\\\n--- run fixtures ---\\\\n'; sed -n '1,400p' research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/run_fixtures.py; printf '\\\\n--- prereg ---\\\\n'; sed -n '1,320p' research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/PREREG_DRAFT_SKELETON.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,150p' docs/research/WP0_TATQA_ADAPTER_CHECKER_CONTRACT_v1.md; printf '\\\\n--- implementation contract ---\\\\n'; sed -n '1,320p' research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/implementation_contract.md; printf '\\\\n--- checker ---\\\\n'; sed -n '1,360p' research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/checker.py; printf '\\\\n--- run fixtures ---\\\\n'; sed -n '1,400p' research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/run_fixtures.py; printf '\\\\n--- prereg ---\\\\n'; sed -n '1,320p' research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/PREREG_DRAFT_SKELETON.md\"","aggregated_output":"# WP-0 TAT-QA Adapter and Checker Contracts v1\n\n> date: 2026-10-13 | author: Loop D (WP-0 item A5) | status: `SPECIFICATION_ONLY - NOT IMPLEMENTED` | revisions 1.1-1.2 (2026-10-13): hidden-gold search clarified and canonicalized (Sec.4-5)\n> parents: [WP0_TATQA_PACKAGE_v1.md](WP0_TATQA_PACKAGE_v1.md), [task card](thesis_experience_v1_task_card.md), [blueprint](THESIS_EXECUTION_BLUEPRINT_v1.md) §2\n> These contracts describe what Loop A must implement in WP-1. Nothing here is code, and nothing here authorises a run.\n\n## 1. Task adapter contract\n\n**Input:** one candidate item from `data/research/tatqa_wp0_2026/candidate_items_v1.json`.\n\n**Actor-visible projection (what the model sees):**\n- the table (all rows and columns, verbatim, no truncation per arm);\n- the two period labels and the row label/identifier needed to name the row;\n- the requested quantity and the requested target unit;\n- the tool description (a deterministic calculator: `calc(expression) -> number`);\n- the arm-specific context block (none for B; the experience block for E/C; the static rules for S).\n\n**Hidden from the actor, always:** `gold_delta_source_unit`, `gold_recompute_rule`, any derived target value, the item's origin id where it would leak the answer, and the whole `candidate_items` file.\n\n**Actor obligations:** choose the row, the two periods, the unit relation and the arithmetic parameter; call the calculator; the final answer must consume the calculator's returned value.\n\n**Answer format (fixed):** `{row: <label>, periods: [<late>, <early>], delta_source: <number>, delta_target: <number>, unit: <target unit>}` in a single JSON object, or the literal token `REFUSED` / `UNKNOWN`.\n\n**Determinism:** the adapter must produce byte-identical prompts for the same item and arm. No timestamps, no sampling, no arm-dependent table truncation.\n\n## 2. Checker contract\n\n**Gold recomputation (independent of the actor):** for the item's `row_index`, read `value(late)` and `value(early)` from the table cells with the stated parser (strip thousands separators, treat parentheses as negative), compute `delta_source = value(late) - value(early)`, then convert by the scale factor between `source_unit` and the requested target unit. The checker must never read the actor's output before the gold exists.\n\n**Scoring (per item, per arm, per repeat):**\n| Outcome | Rule |\n|---|---|\n| `correct` | `delta_source` and `delta_target` both match gold exactly (after the declared rounding); row and periods match |\n| `correct_other_form` | same value via a mathematically equivalent expression (e.g., early-minus-late with a negated sign) - counted as correct, and recorded separately |\n| `wrong_unit` | `delta_source` correct but `delta_target` wrong |\n| `wrong_period` | the periods chosen differ from the item's |\n| `regressed` | compared to arm B on the same item, a previously correct answer becomes incorrect |\n| `refused` | the literal `REFUSED` |\n| `unknown` | the literal `UNKNOWN`, a timeout, or an unparseable answer |\n\n**Independent unit of analysis:** the origin (the raw record), not the item, not the repeat. Report per-origin paired differences `E-B`, `E-C`, `E-S`, `C-B`, with the origin-level differences listed explicitly.\n\n**Anti-leakage obligations the checker must enforce:** (a) the item's gold appears nowhere in the actor-visible projection; (b) no item shares an origin with any experience episode used in the same arm run; (c) the C-arm context differs from the E-arm context by at most 5% in context tokens; (d) the S-arm rules are frozen at development time and never edited per item.\n\n## 3. Fixture obligations (what Loop A must demonstrate without any model)\n\nOn synthetic fixtures only, Loop A must show:\n1. the adapter emits the same prompt twice for the same item (byte equality);\n2. the gold never appears in the projection (string search);\n3. the checker's recomputation matches hand-computed values on at least 5 hand-built fixtures, including one with parentheses-negative cells and one with a thousands separator;\n4. the scale conversion matches for thousand->unit, million->thousand, billion->million and percent->percent;\n5. an `UNKNOWN` and a `REFUSED` answer are classified correctly;\n6. the arm-context token delta between E and C is computed and reported.\n\n**Stop:** if any fixture obligation cannot be met, WP-1 stops and reports `SOFTWARE_NOT_QUALIFIED`. No model is called to \"try it out\".\n\n## 4. Revision 1.1 (2026-10-13): hidden-gold search clarified\n\n**Trigger:** WP-1 run 1 (`tatqa-wp1-20261013`) stopped fail-closed with `SOFTWARE_NOT_QUALIFIED: hidden_gold_search`. Diagnosis: the check searched `late_value` and `early_value` (fields of the `expected_gold` object) inside the projection. Those are raw table cells that the actor must read to compute the delta, so the search necessarily hits the table itself - a false-positive class, not a leak. The fail-closed stop was correct behaviour; the check definition, as written, was over-broad and undecidable.\n\n**Revision (supersedes Sec.3 obligation 2 only; every other obligation is unchanged):**\n\n(a) Forbidden-name search: none of the hidden field names (`gold_delta_source_unit`, `gold_recompute_rule`, `gold_delta_target_unit`, `expected_gold`, `origin_id`, `item_id`) appears in the projection.\n(b) Answer-value search: the derived answer strings - `delta_source` and `delta_target` exactly as the checker renders them (for example `60`, `-55`, `1.3`, `1300`) - have ZERO boundary-aware matches in the full serialized projection. A match counts only when flanked on both sides by characters outside the set {digits, `.`, `,`, `+`, `-`} (string start/end count as a boundary). No length filter; applies to EVERY fixture.\n(c) `late_value` and `early_value` are excluded from the search set: they are actor-visible task inputs by design, not gold.\n(d) Fixture-design precondition (makes (b) informative rather than vacuous): for every fixture, the same boundary-aware search over the raw table cells and period labels alone must also find zero matches; if a collision exists, the fixture's synthetic numbers must be adjusted (keeping the arithmetic correct) - never the check.\n\n**Change control:** this revision does not weaken (a)-(d); it makes the search well-defined and extends its scope to all fixtures. Any further failure of this obligation after this revision is a genuine finding.\n\n## 5. Revision 1.2 (2026-10-13): leak-guard canonicalization + taxonomy/receipt precision\n\n**Trigger:** Loop C WP-1 audit (`tatqa-wp1-audit-20261013`, CONDITIONAL) found: (i) the hidden-gold needle rendered `1300.0` where 1.1(b) names `1300` (latent false-negative, positive-control proven); (ii) the emitted outcome vocabulary (`wrong`) is a superset of the declared taxonomy, and `regressed` excludes refused/unknown; (iii) safety booleans are recorded as literal self-attestation rather than derived evidence; (iv) `FIXTURE_RECEIPT` has no integrity pin and its canonical path needs stating; (v) `target_unit` is absent from all 60 frozen candidates (identity conversions only) and `gold_delta_source_unit` is a naming trap - both to be resolved at prereg/item-freeze.\n\n**Revision (supersedes 1.1(b),(d); extends the taxonomy; nothing is weakened):**\n\n(a) **Chosen form.** The answer-value needle is the canonical plain-decimal form of `delta_source` and `delta_target`: no trailing zeros, no exponent (for example `60`, `-55`, `1.3`, `3`, `1300`). Where the exact `str(value)` render differs (for example `1300.0`), BOTH forms are searched.\n(b) **Positive control (mandatory).** The check must include a self-test that injects each needle into a synthetic projection and asserts the guard fires; a guard that cannot catch its own injected leak fails the obligation. At minimum cover the `1300`/`1300.0` pair and one negative value.\n(c) **Coverage.** The byte-determinism obligation applies to EVERY fixture and ALL four arms (B/E/C/S), not one item and one arm.\n(d) **Outcome vocabulary (eight classes).** `correct`, `correct_other_form`, `wrong_unit`, `wrong_period`, `wrong` (answered and parseable, neither correct nor a specific wrong_* class), `regressed`, `refused`, `unknown`. `regressed` is assigned by the B-vs-arm comparison when a B-correct outcome becomes non-correct other than `refused`/`unknown`; refusals and unknowns remain first-class.\n(e) **Receipts.** Every safety boolean is either derived from executed behaviour or explicitly labelled `attested: true`; `scoring_inputs_all_synthetic` must be derived. `WP1_RECEIPT.artifact_hashes` must include the `FIXTURE_RECEIPT` hash. The canonical `FIXTURE_RECEIPT` path is `data/research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/FIXTURE_RECEIPT.json`; the copy under `research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/` is a byte-identical mirror for tracking.\n(f) **Known traps recorded for the prereg.** `gold_delta_source_unit` stores a delta VALUE in source units (the name is not a unit string); `target_unit` is absent from the frozen candidate items, so every conversion is currently the identity - a target-unit assignment decision is PENDING at item freeze.\n--- implementation contract ---\n# WP-1 Implementation Contract\n\nTask: `tatqa_wp1_loop_a`\n\nScope: implement the thin checker, deterministic adapter, synthetic fixture runner, preflight receipt, and preregistration draft for TAT-QA WP-1. This contract authorizes no candidate-item scoring, model call, endpoint call, episode collection, training, service access, database access, network access, commit, or push.\n\nWrite paths:\n\n- `research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/`\n- `data/research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/`\n\nRuntime and style:\n\n- Python 3.12 standard library only.\n- UTF-8 input and LF-terminated JSON/Markdown outputs.\n- Synthetic fixtures only for execution.\n- Fail closed if any fixture obligation or preflight check fails.\n\n## 1. Module list and signatures\n\n### `research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/checker.py`\n\n```python\nSCALES: dict[str, Decimal]\nREQUIRED_RUNTIME_FIELDS: frozenset[str]\nCORRECT_OUTCOMES: frozenset[str]\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass Gold:\n    late_value: Decimal\n    early_value: Decimal\n    delta_source: Decimal\n    delta_target: Decimal\n    source_unit: str\n    target_unit: str\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass PreparedItem:\n    item_id: str\n    origin_id: str\n    row_label: str\n    late_period: str\n    early_period: str\n    gold: Gold\n\ndef normalize_unit(unit: str | None) -> str: ...\ndef parse_numeric_cell(value: str | int | float) -> Decimal: ...\ndef conversion_factor(source_unit: str, target_unit: str) -> Decimal: ...\ndef recompute_gold(item: Mapping[str, Any]) -> Gold: ...\ndef prepare_item(item: Mapping[str, Any]) -> PreparedItem: ...\ndef parse_answer(answer_text: str) -> dict[str, Any] | None: ...\ndef score_prepared(prepared: PreparedItem, answer_text: str) -> dict[str, str]: ...\ndef score_item(item: Mapping[str, Any], answer_text: str) -> dict[str, str]: ...\ndef apply_regression(base_outcome: str, arm_outcome: str) -> str: ...\ndef aggregate_outcomes(records: Iterable[Mapping[str, Any]]) -> dict[str, Any]: ...\ndef paired_origin_differences(\n    records: Iterable[Mapping[str, Any]],\n    left_arm: str,\n    right_arm: str,\n) -> dict[str, Any]: ...\n```\n\nGold construction is separated from answer parsing. `score_item` constructs `PreparedItem` before it passes `answer_text` into `score_prepared`. Numeric parsing removes thousands separators and treats surrounding parentheses as negative. Supported scale keys are `unit`, `thousand`, `million`, `billion`, and `percent`; conversion uses the ratio of their scale exponents.\n\nOutcome precedence:\n\n1. Literal `REFUSED` -> `refused`.\n2. Literal `UNKNOWN`, timeout marker, or unparseable JSON -> `unknown`.\n3. Row mismatch -> `wrong`.\n4. Reversed period order with both values negated -> `correct_other_form`.\n5. Any other period mismatch -> `wrong_period`.\n6. Source value correct and target value wrong -> `wrong_unit`.\n7. Both values correct -> `correct`.\n8. Otherwise -> `wrong`.\n\n`regressed` is assigned only by `apply_regression` when a B outcome in `{correct, correct_other_form}` becomes a non-correct answer other than `refused` or `unknown`; refusals and unknowns remain first-class.\n\n### `research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/adapter.py`\n\n```python\nARMS: frozenset[str]\nCONTEXT_HOOK_TYPES: Mapping[str, str]\nANSWER_FORMAT: str\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass ContextHook:\n    arm: str\n    hook_type: str\n    text: str\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass Projection:\n    row_label: str\n    period_late: str\n    period_early: str\n    source_unit: str\n    target_unit: str\n    requested_quantity: str\n    table: list[list[str]]\n\ndef runtime_payload_from_candidate(item: Mapping[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]: ...\ndef projection_from_candidate(item: Mapping[str, Any]) -> Projection: ...\ndef validate_context_hook(hook: ContextHook) -> None: ...\ndef build_prompt(item: Mapping[str, Any], hook: ContextHook) -> str: ...\ndef count_context_tokens(text: str) -> int: ...\ndef context_token_delta(\n    e_text: str,\n    c_text: str,\n    relative_limit: Decimal = Decimal(\"0.05\"),\n) -> dict[str, Any]: ...\n```\n\nThe prompt is deterministic UTF-8 JSON text with no timestamp, random value, item id, origin id, gold field, gold value key, or hidden recomputation rule. The complete table is serialized without truncation. Arm hooks are typed as `none`, `experience`, `matched_experience`, or `static_rules`; the adapter serializes supplied typed placeholder text and does not construct real experience blocks.\n\nToken accounting uses a documented deterministic lexical proxy: non-whitespace tokens from `re.findall(r\"\\\\S+\", text)`. It is not a model tokenizer estimate.\n\n### `research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/provenance.py`\n\n```python\nTASK: str\n\ndef task_provenance() -> dict[str, Any]: ...\ndef attributed_payload(payload: Mapping[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]: ...\ndef write_json_lf(path: str | Path, payload: Mapping[str, Any]) -> None: ...\n```\n\nThe writer attributes every generated receipt to `tatqa_wp1_loop_a`, records `model_calls=0`, and records `endpoint_calls=0`.\n\n### `research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/run_fixtures.py`\n\n```python\nWORK_DIR: Path\nDATA_OUT_DIR: Path\nFIXTURE_PATH: Path\n\ndef load_synthetic_fixtures() -> dict[str, Any]: ...\ndef fixture_item(fixture: Mapping[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]: ...\ndef run_checks(fixtures: Mapping[str, Any]) -> tuple[list[dict[str, Any]], dict[str, Any]]: ...\ndef write_outputs(fixtures: Mapping[str, Any], obligations: list[dict[str, Any]], metrics: dict[str, Any]) -> None: ...\ndef main() -> int: ...\n```\n\n### `research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/fixtures/synthetic_fixtures.json`\n\nSchema: `tatqa_wp1_synthetic_fixtures_v1`.\n\nRequired fixtures:\n\n- `normal_unit`: ordinary two-cell recomputation.\n- `parentheses_negative`: parenthesized early value becomes negative.\n- `thousands_separator`: comma-separated cells are parsed as thousands separators.\n- `thousand_to_unit`\n- `million_to_thousand`\n- `billion_to_million`\n- `percent_to_percent`\n\nThe first seven fixtures provide seven hand-built recomputations, including the two mandated parsing cases and all four mandated conversions. Answer fixtures cover `correct`, `correct_other_form`, `wrong_unit`, `wrong_period`, `refused`, and `unknown`.\n\nThe E and C placeholder contexts are synthetic strings with a measured lexical token delta declared in the fixture file. They are not episodes and are not real experience blocks.\n\n## 2. Fixture obligations\n\n`run_fixtures.py` must execute exactly these six obligations and emit one result object per obligation:\n\n1. `prompt_byte_determinism`: build the same synthetic item plus identical hook twice and compare encoded UTF-8 bytes.\n2. `hidden_gold_search`: reject hidden key names and ensure the expected gold decimal strings are absent from the actor-visible prompt.\n3. `gold_recomputation`: compare `recompute_gold` results to at least five hand-computed expected values, including parentheses-negative and thousands-separator cases.\n4. `scale_conversions`: compare all four specified unit conversions.\n5. `unknown_and_refused`: classify literal `UNKNOWN` and `REFUSED` correctly, plus unparseable JSON as unknown.\n6. `ec_token_delta`: compute lexical token counts, absolute delta, relative delta, and pass/fail against the fixture's 5% limit.\n\nAdditional non-obligation synthetic checks are permitted only to exercise the declared checker taxonomy, regression helper, provenance writer, and metric pipeline. They must use fixture origin/item ids only.\n\n## 3. Preflight schema\n\n`research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/PREFLIGHT_RECEIPT.json` uses schema `tatqa_wp1_preflight_receipt_v1` and contains:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"schema\": \"tatqa_wp1_preflight_receipt_v1\",\n  \"task\": \"tatqa_wp1_loop_a\",\n  \"status\": \"PASS\",\n  \"provenance\": {},\n  \"required_files\": {},\n  \"runtime_schema\": {},\n  \"checker_domain\": {},\n  \"identifier_resolution\": {},\n  \"metric_pipeline\": {},\n  \"held_out_result_read\": false,\n  \"checks\": []\n}\n```\n\nThe preflight reads only the pinned candidate/origin metadata needed to validate structure, field names, checker-domain coverage, and identifier resolution. It does not call `recompute_gold`, `score_item`, or any metric on candidate items and does not read any candidate gold field.\n\n## 4. Generated receipt schemas\n\n`data/research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/FIXTURE_RECEIPT.json` uses schema `tatqa_wp1_fixture_receipt_v1` and contains `task`, `status`, `provenance`, `obligations`, `taxonomy_checks`, `regression_check`, `metric_pipeline`, `cost`, and `deviations`.\n\n`research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/PREREG_DRAFT_SKELETON.md` is a draft-only Markdown file. Actor revision, model, settings, real episode context, analysis implementation, budget/window, and advisor/owner decisions remain exactly `PENDING`.\n\n`research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/WP1_RECEIPT.json` uses schema `tatqa_wp1_receipt_v1` and contains:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task\": \"tatqa_wp1_loop_a\",\n  \"status\": \"PASS\",\n  \"start_utc\": \"YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ\",\n  \"end_utc\": \"YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ\",\n  \"input_verification\": {\n    \"hashes\": {},\n    \"counts\": {},\n    \"status\": \"PASS\"\n  },\n  \"artifact_hashes\": {\n    \"checker\": \"\",\n    \"adapter\": \"\",\n    \"fixtures\": \"\",\n    \"preflight\": \"\",\n    \"contract\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"fixture_results\": [],\n  \"preflight_results\": [],\n  \"cost\": {\n    \"model_calls\": 0,\n    \"endpoint_calls\": 0\n  },\n  \"unverified_items\": [],\n  \"deviations\": []\n}\n```\n\n## 5. Exact commands\n\nThe implementation must not run a model, endpoint, service, database, training command, network command, loop verifier, commit, or push.\n\nAfter this contract is written, hash it before creating or running implementation files:\n\n```bash\ncd /home/testuser/wzh/projects/agents_final_tech\nsha256sum research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/implementation_contract.md > research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/implementation_contract.sha256\nsha256sum -c research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/implementation_contract.sha256\n```\n\nImplementation and validation:\n\n```bash\ncd /home/testuser/wzh/projects/agents_final_tech\npython3 -m py_compile research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/checker.py research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/adapter.py research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/provenance.py research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/run_fixtures.py\npython3 research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/run_fixtures.py\npython3 -m json.tool research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/PREFLIGHT_RECEIPT.json >/dev/null\npython3 -m json.tool data/research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/FIXTURE_RECEIPT.json >/dev/null\npython3 -m json.tool research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/WP1_RECEIPT.json >/dev/null\n```\n\nFinal artifact verification:\n\n```bash\ncd /home/testuser/wzh/projects/agents_final_tech\nsha256sum research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/checker.py research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/adapter.py research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/fixtures/synthetic_fixtures.json research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/PREFLIGHT_RECEIPT.json research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/implementation_contract.md\ngit status --short -- research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1 data/research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1\n```\n\n## 6. Stop conditions\n\n- Pinned input hash mismatch: report `HASH_MISMATCH` and stop.\n- Any of the six fixture obligations fails: report `SOFTWARE_NOT_QUALIFIED` with the failed obligation and stop without changing the fixture to force a pass.\n- Any required forbidden action: stop and report the blocked requirement.\n- No scientific result, pilot result, candidate-item score, or held-out outcome is permitted in any receipt.\n\n## 7. Revision 1.1 completion addendum (2026-10-13)\n\nRun 1 (`tatqa-wp1-20261013`) failed closed on `hidden_gold_search` because the original check searched the actor-visible raw cells `late_value` and `early_value`. Revision 1.1 of the governing contract supersedes only that obligation.\n\nThe run-2 implementation of `hidden_gold_search`:\n\n- retains the exact forbidden-name search from run 1;\n- searches only the checker-rendered `delta_source` and `delta_target` strings;\n- applies boundary-aware matching to the full serialized actor-visible projection for every fixture, requiring zero matches and applying no length filter;\n- excludes `late_value` and `early_value` from the answer-value search set;\n- requires the same boundary-aware search to return zero matches over raw table cells and period labels alone for every fixture, so the search is non-vacuous.\n\nThe seven synthetic fixture numbers require no adjustment because all seven satisfy the fixture-design precondition. No checker, adapter, provenance module, pinned input, or scientific item was changed.\n\nRun 2 uses run id `tatqa-wp1b-20261013`. On a passing run it emits these artifacts:\n\n- `research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/PREFLIGHT_RECEIPT.json`\n- `data/research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/FIXTURE_RECEIPT.json`\n- `research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/WP1_RECEIPT.json`\n\nThe generated receipts carry zero model and endpoint calls, per-obligation results, the requested artifact hashes, unverified items, and deviations. This addendum does not change any other obligation or stop condition.\n\n--- checker ---\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nimport re\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom decimal import Decimal, InvalidOperation\nfrom typing import Any, Iterable, Mapping\n\n\nSCALES: dict[str, Decimal] = {\n    \"unit\": Decimal(0),\n    \"thousand\": Decimal(3),\n    \"million\": Decimal(6),\n    \"billion\": Decimal(9),\n    \"percent\": Decimal(0),\n}\nUNIT_ALIASES: dict[str, str] = {\n    \"\": \"unit\",\n    \"unit\": \"unit\",\n    \"units\": \"unit\",\n    \"none\": \"unit\",\n    \"thousand\": \"thousand\",\n    \"thousands\": \"thousand\",\n    \"million\": \"million\",\n    \"millions\": \"million\",\n    \"billion\": \"billion\",\n    \"billions\": \"billion\",\n    \"percent\": \"percent\",\n    \"%\": \"percent\",\n}\nREQUIRED_RUNTIME_FIELDS: frozenset[str] = frozenset(\n    {\n        \"table\",\n        \"row_index\",\n        \"period_late\",\n        \"period_early\",\n        \"source_unit\",\n        \"target_unit\",\n        \"requested_quantity\",\n    }\n)\nCORRECT_OUTCOMES: frozenset[str] = frozenset({\"correct\", \"correct_other_form\"})\nNUMERIC_CELL_PATTERN = re.compile(\n    r\"^\\s*\\(?\\s*[+-]?(?:\\d{1,3}(?:,\\d{3})+|\\d+)(?:\\.\\d+)?\\s*%?\\s*\\)?$\"\n)\nTIMEOUT_TOKENS: frozenset[str] = frozenset(\n    {\"TIMEOUT\", \"TIMEOUT_EXCEEDED\", \"TIMEOUT_ERROR\"}\n)\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass Gold:\n    late_value: Decimal\n    early_value: Decimal\n    delta_source: Decimal\n    delta_target: Decimal\n    source_unit: str\n    target_unit: str\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass PreparedItem:\n    item_id: str\n    origin_id: str\n    row_label: str\n    late_period: str\n    early_period: str\n    gold: Gold\n\n\ndef normalize_unit(unit: str | None) -> str:\n    if unit is None:\n        return \"unit\"\n    if not isinstance(unit, str):\n        raise ValueError(\"unit must be a string or null\")\n    key = unit.strip().lower()\n    if key not in UNIT_ALIASES:\n        raise ValueError(f\"unsupported unit: {unit!r}\")\n    return UNIT_ALIASES[key]\n\n\ndef parse_numeric_cell(value: str | int | float) -> Decimal:\n    if isinstance(value, bool):\n        raise ValueError(\"boolean is not a numeric table cell\")\n    negative = False\n    if isinstance(value, Decimal):\n        parsed = value\n    elif isinstance(value, int):\n        parsed = Decimal(value)\n    elif isinstance(value, float):\n        parsed = Decimal(str(value))\n    elif isinstance(value, str):\n        text = value.strip()\n        if not NUMERIC_CELL_PATTERN.fullmatch(text):\n            raise ValueError(f\"invalid numeric table cell: {value!r}\")\n        negative = text.startswith(\"(\") and text.endswith(\")\")\n        if negative:\n            text = text[1:-1].strip()\n        if text.endswith(\"%\"):\n            text = text[:-1].strip()\n        text = text.replace(\",\", \"\")\n        try:\n            parsed = Decimal(text)\n        except InvalidOperation as exc:\n            raise ValueError(f\"invalid numeric table cell: {value!r}\") from exc\n    else:\n        raise ValueError(f\"unsupported numeric table cell type: {type(value).__name__}\")\n    if not parsed.is_finite():\n        raise ValueError(\"numeric table cell must be finite\")\n    if negative:\n        parsed = -parsed\n    return parsed\n\n\ndef conversion_factor(source_unit: str, target_unit: str) -> Decimal:\n    source_key = normalize_unit(source_unit)\n    target_key = normalize_unit(target_unit)\n    allowed = source_key == target_key or {\n        (source_key, target_key)\n    }.issubset(\n        {\n            (\"thousand\", \"unit\"),\n            (\"million\", \"thousand\"),\n            (\"billion\", \"million\"),\n            (\"percent\", \"percent\"),\n        }\n    )\n    if not allowed:\n        raise ValueError(\n            f\"unsupported unit conversion: {source_key!r} -> {target_key!r}\"\n        )\n    exponent = SCALES[source_key] - SCALES[target_key]\n    return Decimal(10) ** exponent\n\n\ndef _required_runtime_payload(item: Mapping[str, Any]) -> None:\n    missing = sorted(field for field in REQUIRED_RUNTIME_FIELDS if field not in item)\n    if missing:\n        raise ValueError(f\"runtime item is missing fields: {missing}\")\n\n\ndef _period_cell(item: Mapping[str, Any], key: str) -> tuple[int, str]:\n    period = item[key]\n    if not isinstance(period, Mapping):\n        raise ValueError(f\"{key} must be an object\")\n    if \"col\" not in period or \"label\" not in period:\n        raise ValueError(f\"{key} must contain col and label\")\n    col = period[\"col\"]\n    label = period[\"label\"]\n    if isinstance(col, bool) or not isinstance(col, int) or col < 0:\n        raise ValueError(f\"{key}.col must be a non-negative integer\")\n    if not isinstance(label, str):\n        raise ValueError(f\"{key}.label must be a string\")\n    return col, label\n\n\ndef recompute_gold(item: Mapping[str, Any]) -> Gold:\n    _required_runtime_payload(item)\n    table = item[\"table\"]\n    if not isinstance(table, list) or not table:\n        raise ValueError(\"table must be a non-empty list\")\n    row_index = item[\"row_index\"]\n    if isinstance(row_index, bool) or not isinstance(row_index, int):\n        raise ValueError(\"row_index must be an integer\")\n    if row_index < 0 or row_index >= len(table):\n        raise ValueError(\"row_index is out of range\")\n    row = table[row_index]\n    if not isinstance(row, list) or not row:\n        raise ValueError(\"selected table row must be a non-empty list\")\n    late_col, _ = _period_cell(item, \"period_late\")\n    early_col, _ = _period_cell(item, \"period_early\")\n    if late_col >= len(row) or early_col >= len(row):\n        raise ValueError(\"period column is out of range for the selected row\")\n    source_unit = normalize_unit(item.get(\"source_unit\"))\n    target_unit = normalize_unit(item.get(\"target_unit\", source_unit))\n    late_value = parse_numeric_cell(row[late_col])\n    early_value = parse_numeric_cell(row[early_col])\n    delta_source = late_value - early_value\n    delta_target = delta_source * conversion_factor(source_unit, target_unit)\n    return Gold(\n        late_value=late_value,\n        early_value=early_value,\n        delta_source=delta_source,\n        delta_target=delta_target,\n        source_unit=source_unit,\n        target_unit=target_unit,\n    )\n\n\ndef prepare_item(item: Mapping[str, Any]) -> PreparedItem:\n    gold = recompute_gold(item)\n    table = item[\"table\"]\n    row_index = item[\"row_index\"]\n    row_label = table[row_index][0]\n    return PreparedItem(\n        item_id=str(item.get(\"item_id\", \"\")),\n        origin_id=str(item.get(\"origin_id\", \"\")),\n        row_label=str(row_label),\n        late_period=str(item[\"period_late\"][\"label\"]),\n        early_period=str(item[\"period_early\"][\"label\"]),\n        gold=gold,\n    )\n\n\ndef _answer_decimal(value: Any, field: str) -> Decimal:\n    if isinstance(value, bool) or not isinstance(value, (int, float, str)):\n        raise ValueError(f\"{field} must be numeric\")\n    try:\n        parsed = Decimal(str(value))\n    except InvalidOperation as exc:\n        raise ValueError(f\"{field} must be numeric\") from exc\n    if not parsed.is_finite():\n        raise ValueError(f\"{field} must be finite\")\n    return parsed\n\n\ndef parse_answer(answer_text: str) -> dict[str, Any] | None:\n    if not isinstance(answer_text, str):\n        return None\n    token = answer_text.strip().upper()\n    if token == \"REFUSED\":\n        return {\"answer_class\": \"refused\"}\n    if token == \"UNKNOWN\" or token in TIMEOUT_TOKENS:\n        return {\"answer_class\": \"unknown\"}\n    try:\n        parsed = json.loads(answer_text)\n    except (json.JSONDecodeError, TypeError):\n        return {\"answer_class\": \"unknown\"}\n    if not isinstance(parsed, dict):\n        return {\"answer_class\": \"unknown\"}\n    required = {\"row\", \"periods\", \"delta_source\", \"delta_target\", \"unit\"}\n    if set(parsed) != required:\n        return {\"answer_class\": \"unknown\"}\n    if not isinstance(parsed[\"row\"], str):\n        return {\"answer_class\": \"unknown\"}\n    periods = parsed[\"periods\"]\n    if (\n        not isinstance(periods, list)\n        or len(periods) != 2\n        or any(not isinstance(period, str) for period in periods)\n    ):\n        return {\"answer_class\": \"unknown\"}\n    if not isinstance(parsed[\"unit\"], str):\n        return {\"answer_class\": \"unknown\"}\n    try:\n        delta_source = _answer_decimal(parsed[\"delta_source\"], \"delta_source\")\n        delta_target = _answer_decimal(parsed[\"delta_target\"], \"delta_target\")\n    except ValueError:\n        return {\"answer_class\": \"unknown\"}\n    return {\n        \"answer_class\": \"parsed\",\n        \"row\": parsed[\"row\"],\n        \"periods\": periods,\n        \"delta_source\": delta_source,\n        \"delta_target\": delta_target,\n        \"unit\": normalize_unit(parsed[\"unit\"]),\n    }\n\n\ndef score_prepared(prepared: PreparedItem, answer_text: str) -> dict[str, str]:\n    answer = parse_answer(answer_text)\n    if answer is None:\n        return {\"outcome\": \"unknown\"}\n    if answer[\"answer_class\"] != \"parsed\":\n        return {\"outcome\": answer[\"answer_class\"]}\n    if answer[\"row\"] != prepared.row_label:\n        return {\"outcome\": \"wrong\"}\n    gold = prepared.gold\n    if (\n        answer[\"periods\"] == [prepared.early_period, prepared.late_period]\n        and answer[\"delta_source\"] == -gold.delta_source\n        and answer[\"delta_target\"] == -gold.delta_target\n    ):\n        return {\"outcome\": \"correct_other_form\"}\n    if answer[\"periods\"] != [prepared.late_period, prepared.early_period]:\n        return {\"outcome\": \"wrong_period\"}\n    source_correct = answer[\"delta_source\"] == gold.delta_source\n    target_correct = answer[\"delta_target\"] == gold.delta_target\n    if source_correct and not target_correct:\n        return {\"outcome\": \"wrong_unit\"}\n    if source_correct and target_correct and answer[\"unit\"] == gold.target_unit:\n        return {\"outcome\": \"correct\"}\n    return {\"outcome\": \"wrong\"}\n\n\ndef score_item(item: Mapping[str, Any], answer_text: str) -> dict[str, str]:\n    prepared = prepare_item(item)\n    return score_prepared(prepared, answer_text)\n\n\ndef apply_regression(base_outcome: str, arm_outcome: str) -> str:\n    if (\n        base_outcome in CORRECT_OUTCOMES\n        and arm_outcome not in CORRECT_OUTCOMES\n        and arm_outcome not in {\"refused\", \"unknown\"}\n    ):\n        return \"regressed\"\n    return arm_outcome\n\n\ndef aggregate_outcomes(records: Iterable[Mapping[str, Any]]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    records_by_arm: dict[str, list[Mapping[str, Any]]] = defaultdict(list)\n    for record in records:\n        required = {\"origin_id\", \"item_id\", \"arm\", \"outcome\"}\n        if not required.issubset(record):\n            raise ValueError(f\"record is missing fields: {sorted(required - set(record))}\")\n        records_by_arm[str(record[\"arm\"])].append(record)\n    arms: dict[str, Any] = {}\n    for arm in sorted(records_by_arm):\n        arm_records = records_by_arm[arm]\n        outcomes = Counter(str(record[\"outcome\"]) for record in arm_records)\n        correct_count = sum(outcomes[outcome] for outcome in CORRECT_OUTCOMES)\n        total = len(arm_records)\n        arms[arm] = {\n            \"total\": total,\n            \"origin_count\": len({str(record[\"origin_id\"]) for record in arm_records}),\n            \"outcome_counts\": dict(sorted(outcomes.items())),\n            \"correct_count\": correct_count,\n            \"correct_rate\": correct_count / total if total else None,\n        }\n    return {\n        \"record_count\": sum(len(value) for value in records_by_arm.values()),\n        \"arms\": arms,\n    }\n\n\ndef _origin_rates(\n    records: Iterable[Mapping[str, Any]], arm: str\n) -> dict[str, tuple[int, int]]:\n    values: dict[str, list[int]] = defaultdict(list)\n    for record in records:\n        if str(record[\"arm\"]) != arm:\n            continue\n        is_correct = str(record[\"outcome\"]) in CORRECT_OUTCOMES\n        values[str(record[\"origin_id\"])].append(int(is_correct))\n    return {\n        origin: (sum(observations), len(observations))\n        for origin, observations in values.items()\n    }\n\n\ndef paired_origin_differences(\n    records: Iterable[Mapping[str, Any]],\n    left_arm: str,\n    right_arm: str,\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    materialized = [dict(record) for record in records]\n    left = _origin_rates(materialized, left_arm)\n    right = _origin_rates(materialized, right_arm)\n    origins = sorted(set(left) | set(right))\n    differences: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n    for origin in origins:\n        left_count, left_total = left.get(origin, (0, 0))\n        right_count, right_total = right.get(origin, (0, 0))\n        left_rate = left_count / left_total if left_total else None\n        right_rate = right_count / right_total if right_total else None\n        delta_pp = (\n            (left_rate - right_rate) * 100\n            if left_rate is not None and right_rate is not None\n\n--- run fixtures ---\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport re\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom decimal import Decimal\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any, Callable, Mapping\n\nimport adapter\nimport checker\nimport provenance\n\n\nWORK_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nREPO_ROOT = WORK_DIR.parents[2]\nDATA_OUT_DIR = REPO_ROOT / \"data/research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1\"\nFIXTURE_PATH = WORK_DIR / \"fixtures/synthetic_fixtures.json\"\nPREFLIGHT_PATH = WORK_DIR / \"PREFLIGHT_RECEIPT.json\"\nFIXTURE_RECEIPT_PATH = DATA_OUT_DIR / \"FIXTURE_RECEIPT.json\"\nPREREG_PATH = WORK_DIR / \"PREREG_DRAFT_SKELETON.md\"\nWP1_RECEIPT_PATH = WORK_DIR / \"WP1_RECEIPT.json\"\nRUN_ID = \"tatqa-wp1b-20261013\"\nSTART_UTC = datetime.now(timezone.utc).strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")\nBOUNDARY_CHARACTERS = frozenset(\"0123456789.,+-\")\nPINNED_INPUTS = {\n    REPO_ROOT / \"data/research/tatqa_wp0_2026/candidate_items_v1.json\": (\n        \"bc55fe7a53381f32e5d84ff6c17ced18ec72fd322f98a9f80c4eccb714caac12\"\n    ),\n    REPO_ROOT / \"data/research/tatqa_wp0_2026/origin_manifest.json\": (\n        \"3718e6fef4d52bec0c1c29b47ba9ab60e298754b9e8527835d09c9d223d70cea\"\n    ),\n    REPO_ROOT / \"data/research/tatqa_raw_2026/tatqa_dataset_train.json\": (\n        \"2df6e722cdbaaa37efcbfb280f5c9a15be29a6ec18f618ef936fe63cc6d07c69\"\n    ),\n    REPO_ROOT / \"data/research/tatqa_raw_2026/tatqa_dataset_dev.json\": (\n        \"8da095a819af6db3c14877c6df2d4d29960e41d1a63dd1fa853507bd2a616af5\"\n    ),\n}\n\n\ndef sha256_file(path: Path) -> str:\n    digest = hashlib.sha256()\n    with path.open(\"rb\") as handle:\n        for chunk in iter(lambda: handle.read(1024 * 1024), b\"\"):\n            digest.update(chunk)\n    return digest.hexdigest()\n\n\ndef load_json(path: Path) -> Any:\n    return json.loads(path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n\n\ndef load_synthetic_fixtures() -> dict[str, Any]:\n    fixtures = load_json(FIXTURE_PATH)\n    if fixtures.get(\"schema\") != \"tatqa_wp1_synthetic_fixtures_v1\":\n        raise ValueError(\"unexpected synthetic fixture schema\")\n    return fixtures\n\n\ndef fixture_item(fixture: Mapping[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return dict(fixture[\"item\"])\n\n\ndef _require(condition: bool, message: str) -> None:\n    if not condition:\n        raise AssertionError(message)\n\n\ndef _obligation(\n    obligation_id: str, check: Callable[[], Mapping[str, Any]]\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    try:\n        evidence = dict(check())\n    except Exception as exc:\n        return {\n            \"id\": obligation_id,\n            \"status\": \"FAIL\",\n            \"error\": f\"{type(exc).__name__}: {exc}\",\n        }\n    return {\n        \"id\": obligation_id,\n        \"status\": \"PASS\",\n        \"evidence\": evidence,\n    }\n\n\ndef _boundary_aware_matches(serialized_text: str, needle: str) -> list[str]:\n    pattern = re.compile(\n        rf\"(?<![{re.escape(''.join(sorted(BOUNDARY_CHARACTERS)))}])\"\n        rf\"{re.escape(needle)}\"\n        rf\"(?![{re.escape(''.join(sorted(BOUNDARY_CHARACTERS)))}])\"\n    )\n    return [match.group(0) for match in pattern.finditer(serialized_text)]\n\n\ndef _raw_projection_values(item: Mapping[str, Any]) -> list[str]:\n    raw_values = [\n        str(cell)\n        for row in item[\"table\"]\n        for cell in row\n    ]\n    raw_values.extend(\n        [\n            str(item[\"period_late\"][\"label\"]),\n            str(item[\"period_early\"][\"label\"]),\n        ]\n    )\n    return raw_values\n\n\ndef _check_prompt_byte_determinism(\n    fixtures: Mapping[str, Any]\n) -> Mapping[str, Any]:\n    fixture = fixtures[\"fixtures\"][0]\n    item = fixture_item(fixture)\n    hook = adapter.ContextHook(\"E\", \"experience\", \"synthetic typed placeholder\")\n    first = adapter.build_prompt(item, hook).encode(\"utf-8\")\n    second = adapter.build_prompt(item, hook).encode(\"utf-8\")\n    _require(first == second, \"same item and arm produced different prompt bytes\")\n    return {\n        \"fixture_id\": fixture[\"fixture_id\"],\n        \"first_sha256\": hashlib.sha256(first).hexdigest(),\n        \"second_sha256\": hashlib.sha256(second).hexdigest(),\n        \"byte_equal\": True,\n        \"bytes\": len(first),\n    }\n\n\ndef _check_hidden_gold_search(fixtures: Mapping[str, Any]) -> Mapping[str, Any]:\n    forbidden_keys = [\n        \"gold_delta_source_unit\",\n        \"gold_recompute_rule\",\n        \"gold_delta_target_unit\",\n        \"expected_gold\",\n        \"origin_id\",\n        \"item_id\",\n    ]\n    results = []\n    for fixture in fixtures[\"fixtures\"]:\n        item = fixture_item(fixture)\n        prompt = adapter.build_prompt(item, adapter.ContextHook(\"B\", \"none\", \"\"))\n        gold = checker.recompute_gold(item)\n        answer_values = {\n            \"delta_source\": str(gold.delta_source),\n            \"delta_target\": str(gold.delta_target),\n        }\n        forbidden_found = [key for key in forbidden_keys if key in prompt]\n        projection_matches = {\n            field: _boundary_aware_matches(prompt, value)\n            for field, value in answer_values.items()\n        }\n        raw_values = _raw_projection_values(item)\n        precondition_matches = {\n            field: [\n                raw_value\n                for raw_value in raw_values\n                if _boundary_aware_matches(raw_value, value)\n            ]\n            for field, value in answer_values.items()\n        }\n        _require(not forbidden_found, f\"{fixture['fixture_id']} hidden keys leaked: {forbidden_found}\")\n        _require(\n            not any(projection_matches.values()),\n            f\"{fixture['fixture_id']} derived answer leaked: {projection_matches}\",\n        )\n        _require(\n            not any(precondition_matches.values()),\n            f\"{fixture['fixture_id']} fixture-design collision: {precondition_matches}\",\n        )\n        results.append(\n            {\n                \"fixture_id\": fixture[\"fixture_id\"],\n                \"forbidden_found\": forbidden_found,\n                \"answer_values\": answer_values,\n                \"projection_matches\": projection_matches,\n                \"fixture_design_precondition_matches\": precondition_matches,\n                \"clean\": True,\n            }\n        )\n    return {\n        \"fixture_count\": len(results),\n        \"forbidden_keys_checked\": forbidden_keys,\n        \"excluded_hidden_fields\": [\"late_value\", \"early_value\"],\n        \"answer_fields_checked\": [\"delta_source\", \"delta_target\"],\n        \"results\": results,\n        \"clean\": True,\n    }\n\n\ndef _check_gold_recomputation(fixtures: Mapping[str, Any]) -> Mapping[str, Any]:\n    results = []\n    for fixture in fixtures[\"fixtures\"]:\n        gold = checker.recompute_gold(fixture_item(fixture))\n        expected = fixture[\"expected_gold\"]\n        comparisons = {\n            \"late_value\": gold.late_value,\n            \"early_value\": gold.early_value,\n            \"delta_source\": gold.delta_source,\n            \"delta_target\": gold.delta_target,\n        }\n        for field, actual in comparisons.items():\n            _require(\n                actual == Decimal(expected[field]),\n                f\"{fixture['fixture_id']} {field}: {actual} != {expected[field]}\",\n            )\n        results.append(\n            {\n                \"fixture_id\": fixture[\"fixture_id\"],\n                \"late_value\": str(gold.late_value),\n                \"early_value\": str(gold.early_value),\n                \"delta_source\": str(gold.delta_source),\n                \"delta_target\": str(gold.delta_target),\n            }\n        )\n    _require(len(results) >= 5, \"fewer than five recomputation fixtures\")\n    fixture_ids = {row[\"fixture_id\"] for row in results}\n    _require(\n        {\"parentheses_negative\", \"thousands_separator\"}.issubset(fixture_ids),\n        \"mandated parsing fixtures are missing\",\n    )\n    return {\n        \"fixture_count\": len(results),\n        \"results\": results,\n        \"mandated_cases_present\": [\n            \"parentheses_negative\",\n            \"thousands_separator\",\n        ],\n    }\n\n\ndef _check_scale_conversions(fixtures: Mapping[str, Any]) -> Mapping[str, Any]:\n    expected_conversions = {\n        \"thousand_to_unit\": Decimal(1000),\n        \"million_to_thousand\": Decimal(1000),\n        \"billion_to_million\": Decimal(1000),\n        \"percent_to_percent\": Decimal(1),\n    }\n    fixture_map = {\n        fixture[\"fixture_id\"]: fixture for fixture in fixtures[\"fixtures\"]\n    }\n    results = []\n    for fixture_id, expected_factor in expected_conversions.items():\n        fixture = fixture_map[fixture_id]\n        item = fixture_item(fixture)\n        actual_factor = checker.conversion_factor(\n            item[\"source_unit\"], item[\"target_unit\"]\n        )\n        gold = checker.recompute_gold(item)\n        _require(\n            actual_factor == expected_factor,\n            f\"{fixture_id} factor {actual_factor} != {expected_factor}\",\n        )\n        _require(\n            gold.delta_target == Decimal(fixture[\"expected_gold\"][\"delta_target\"]),\n            f\"{fixture_id} converted gold mismatch\",\n        )\n        results.append(\n            {\n                \"fixture_id\": fixture_id,\n                \"source_unit\": item[\"source_unit\"],\n                \"target_unit\": item[\"target_unit\"],\n                \"factor\": str(actual_factor),\n                \"delta_source\": str(gold.delta_source),\n                \"delta_target\": str(gold.delta_target),\n            }\n        )\n    return {\n        \"conversion_count\": len(results),\n        \"required_conversions\": list(expected_conversions),\n        \"results\": results,\n    }\n\n\ndef _check_unknown_and_refused(\n    fixtures: Mapping[str, Any]\n) -> Mapping[str, Any]:\n    fixture = fixtures[\"fixtures\"][0]\n    item = fixture_item(fixture)\n    cases = [\n        (\"unknown\", \"UNKNOWN\", \"unknown\"),\n        (\"refused\", \"REFUSED\", \"refused\"),\n        (\"unparseable\", fixture[\"answers\"][\"unparseable\"], \"unknown\"),\n    ]\n    results = []\n    for case_id, answer, expected in cases:\n        actual = checker.score_item(item, answer)[\"outcome\"]\n        _require(actual == expected, f\"{case_id}: {actual} != {expected}\")\n        results.append(\n            {\n                \"case_id\": case_id,\n                \"answer\": answer,\n                \"expected\": expected,\n                \"actual\": actual,\n            }\n        )\n    return {\"case_count\": len(results), \"results\": results}\n\n\ndef _check_ec_token_delta(fixtures: Mapping[str, Any]) -> Mapping[str, Any]:\n    context = fixtures[\"context_delta_fixture\"]\n    result = adapter.context_token_delta(\n        context[\"e_context\"],\n        context[\"c_context\"],\n        Decimal(context[\"relative_limit\"]),\n    )\n    _require(\n        result[\"within_limit\"],\n        f\"E/C token delta exceeds limit: {result}\",\n    )\n    return result\n\n\ndef _check_taxonomy(fixtures: Mapping[str, Any]) -> Mapping[str, Any]:\n    fixture = fixtures[\"fixtures\"][0]\n    item = fixture_item(fixture)\n    expected = {\n        \"correct\": \"correct\",\n        \"correct_other_form\": \"correct_other_form\",\n        \"wrong_unit\": \"wrong_unit\",\n        \"wrong_period\": \"wrong_period\",\n        \"refused\": \"refused\",\n        \"unknown\": \"unknown\",\n        \"unparseable\": \"unknown\",\n    }\n    results = []\n    for case_id, expected_outcome in expected.items():\n        actual = checker.score_item(item, fixture[\"answers\"][case_id])[\"outcome\"]\n        _require(\n            actual == expected_outcome,\n            f\"taxonomy {case_id}: {actual} != {expected_outcome}\",\n        )\n        results.append(\n            {\n                \"case_id\": case_id,\n                \"expected\": expected_outcome,\n                \"actual\": actual,\n            }\n        )\n    return {\"case_count\": len(results), \"results\": results}\n\n\ndef _check_regression(fixtures: Mapping[str, Any]) -> Mapping[str, Any]:\n    cases = [\n        (\"correct\", \"wrong_unit\", \"regressed\"),\n        (\"correct_other_form\", \"wrong_period\", \"regressed\"),\n        (\"correct\", \"refused\", \"refused\"),\n        (\"correct\", \"unknown\", \"unknown\"),\n        (\"wrong_unit\", \"correct\", \"correct\"),\n    ]\n    results = []\n    for base, arm, expected in cases:\n        actual = checker.apply_regression(base, arm)\n        _require(actual == expected, f\"regression {base}->{arm}: {actual}\")\n        results.append(\n            {\n                \"base_outcome\": base,\n                \"arm_outcome\": arm,\n                \"expected\": expected,\n                \"actual\": actual,\n            }\n        )\n    return {\"case_count\": len(results), \"results\": results}\n\n\ndef _run_metric_pipeline(fixtures: Mapping[str, Any]) -> Mapping[str, Any]:\n    normal = fixtures[\"fixtures\"][0]\n    thousands = fixtures[\"fixtures\"][2]\n    records = [\n        {\n            \"origin_id\": normal[\"origin_id\"],\n            \"item_id\": normal[\"item\"][\"item_id\"],\n            \"arm\": \"B\",\n            \"outcome\": \"correct\",\n        },\n        {\n            \"origin_id\": normal[\"origin_id\"],\n            \"item_id\": normal[\"item\"][\"item_id\"],\n            \"arm\": \"E\",\n            \"outcome\": \"wrong_unit\",\n        },\n        {\n            \"origin_id\": normal[\"origin_id\"],\n            \"item_id\": normal[\"item\"][\"item_id\"],\n            \"arm\": \"C\",\n            \"outcome\": \"correct\",\n        },\n        {\n            \"origin_id\": normal[\"origin_id\"],\n            \"item_id\": normal[\"item\"][\"item_id\"],\n            \"arm\": \"S\",\n            \"outcome\": \"correct\",\n        },\n        {\n            \"origin_id\": thousands[\"origin_id\"],\n            \"item_id\": thousands[\"item\"][\"item_id\"],\n            \"arm\": \"B\",\n            \"outcome\": \"wrong_unit\",\n        },\n\n--- prereg ---\n# TAT-QA WP-2 Preregistration Draft Skeleton\n\nStatus: `DRAFT - NOT READY - NO PILOT AUTHORIZATION`\n\nTask: `tatqa_wp1_loop_a`\n\nThis skeleton freezes no experiment and authorizes no model call. All actor, context, budget, window, and governance fields remain pending until owner/advisor selection and approval.\n\n## 1. Scientific scope\n\n- Question: whether fixed, related real execution experience changes performance on new-origin two-period table-calculation tasks.\n- Independent unit: origin.\n- Arms: B, E, C, S as defined by the frozen evaluation protocol.\n- Primary outcomes: `correct`, `correct_other_form`, `wrong_unit`, `wrong_period`, `regressed`, `refused`, and `unknown`.\n- No training, memory write-back, pilot execution, or candidate-item scoring is authorized by WP-1.\n\n## 2. Frozen software pins\n\n- Checker: `1dbaa0055fb235d242dc6d4d8f7adade55305c89d4c8673d328348ab21ddb723`\n- Adapter: `dbb5b55bbe48c36c9b5854dfe1780e3a9ca09e08ffe58331468d61ce21f52477`\n- Synthetic fixtures: `8b464f682c8ebd4004fd216b4cd69dc26bcff790c6a035fe2b2f03564d8d2345`\n- Preflight receipt: `b6997cfdf54e25a8679abf00df3d8bc9bccd8a7cdc7b7abead89846c06491931`\n- Implementation contract: `e281248058467de32087ae2ae4138d7506960a96f862154cff1c32ccfb740d06`\n\n## 3. Actor freeze\n\n- Actor revision: `PENDING`\n- Model identity: `PENDING`\n- Model settings: `PENDING`\n- Calculator/tool implementation hash: `PENDING`\n- Adapter settings: `PENDING`\n\n## 4. Experience context\n\n- Episode-source contract: `PENDING`\n- Real E blocks: `PENDING`\n- Real C blocks: `PENDING`\n- Origin-disjointness receipt: `PENDING`\n- Near-duplicate isolation receipt: `PENDING`\n- E/C token-delta receipt: `PENDING`\n- S rules: `PENDING`\n\n## 5. Evaluation and analysis\n\n- Frozen item/split receipt: `PENDING`\n- Pilot task list: `PENDING`\n- Repeat count and ordering: `PENDING`\n- Analysis script hash: `PENDING`\n- Bootstrap method and seed: `PENDING`\n- Origin-level difference table: `PENDING`\n\n## 6. Budget, window, and governance\n\n- Owner authorization: `PENDING`\n- Advisor authorization: `PENDING`\n- Budget/window binding: `PENDING`\n- Start/end UTC: `PENDING`\n- Model-call budget: `PENDING`\n- Endpoint-call budget: `PENDING`\n- Judge-call budget: `0`\n\n## 7. Stop rules\n\n- Leakage or bridge failure: `STOP_THIS_PANEL`\n- B ceiling on both repeats: `STOP_THIS_PANEL`\n- Any unauthorized model, judge, endpoint, database, or service call: stop and report.\n- Fixture or checker failure: report `SOFTWARE_NOT_QUALIFIED`; never weaken the failing test.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
