{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/loop_a_prompt_fix1.md; printf '\\\\n--- audit prompt ---\\\\n'; cat research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/loop_c_wp1_audit_prompt.md; printf '\\\\n--- dispatch entries ---\\\\n'; rg -n 'tatqa-wp1|WP-1|wp1b|wp1-20261013' logs/graph/dispatch_log.md memory/STATE.md memory/THREADS.md | tail -n 120\"","aggregated_output":"# Loop A Assignment - TAT-QA WP-1b (bounded fix + completion; NO MODEL CALLS)\n\nCARD: research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/loop_a_prompt_fix1.md | dispatched 2026-10-13 by Loop D after run-1 fail-closed.\nROLE: Loop A / GB10. Bounded completion of WP-1 after run 1 (`tatqa-wp1-20261013`) stopped with `SOFTWARE_NOT_QUALIFIED: hidden_gold_search`. Nothing else. Model calls = 0.\n\nCONTEXT (read first; binding):\n- Revision 1.1 in `docs/research/WP0_TATQA_ADAPTER_CHECKER_CONTRACT_v1.md` Sec.4 SUPERSEDES Sec.3 obligation 2 only. Run-1 diagnosis: the check searched `late_value`/`early_value` (actor-visible table cells by design) inside the projection -> guaranteed false positive; the fail-closed stop was correct behaviour.\n- Run-1 artifacts remain in `research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/`; do not delete them (extend where the fix requires).\n- Pinned inputs unchanged; re-verify the four hashes and the two counts before running (same as run 1).\n\nTASK (bounded):\n1. Update `_check_hidden_gold_search` in `run_fixtures.py` to revision 1.1:\n   (a) forbidden-name search as before;\n   (b) boundary-aware search for the `delta_source` and `delta_target` strings (as the checker renders them) across the FULL serialized projection for EVERY fixture - zero matches required; flanking characters outside {digits, `.`, `,`, `+`, `-`}; no length filter;\n   (c) exclude `late_value`/`early_value` from the search set;\n   (d) verify the fixture-design precondition per fixture (same boundary-aware search over raw table cells and period labels alone); if a collision exists, adjust ONLY the synthetic fixture numbers (keep the arithmetic correct).\n2. Keep every other check and module unchanged. If the updated suite reveals any other genuine failure, stop and report it - do not weaken anything.\n3. Re-run `python3 research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/run_fixtures.py`. On PASS emit:\n   - `research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/PREFLIGHT_RECEIPT.json`\n   - `data/research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/FIXTURE_RECEIPT.json`\n   - `research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/WP1_RECEIPT.json`\n   (schemas: per-obligation results, artifact hashes for checker/adapter/provenance/run_fixtures/fixtures/contract/preflight, cost model_calls=0, unverified items, deviations; run id `tatqa-wp1b-20261013`.)\n4. Update `implementation_contract.md` with a revision addendum (corrected check + run-2 artifacts) and refresh `implementation_contract.sha256`; update the hash pins in `PREREG_DRAFT_SKELETON.md`.\n5. Same write paths and forbidden list as run 1: no model/judge calls, no network, no services, no training, no commit/push, no edits to paper/, docs/, or pinned inputs, no candidate-item scoring (fixtures are synthetic).\n\nSTOP CONDITIONS: any genuine obligation failure -> `SOFTWARE_NOT_QUALIFIED` naming the failing item (never adjust a test to pass); hash mismatch -> `HASH_MISMATCH`; a forbidden action being required -> stop and report.\n\nEND: final message = status + receipt paths + one-line summary.\n\n--- audit prompt ---\n# Loop C independent audit (read-only) - TAT-QA WP-1 (checker + adapter + fixtures + preflight)\n\nYou are **Loop C**: an independent reviewer. READ-ONLY: do not modify files, commit, push, create runners, or call services. Do not trust the prompt or any summary; verify from the artifacts.\n\nRepo root: `wzh/projects/agents_final_tech`\n\n## Context\nLoop A implemented the WP-1 thin runner under owner approval: run 1 (`tatqa-wp1-20261013`) stopped fail-closed on the hidden-gold check (over-broad search set; correct stop); spec revision 1.1 clarified the check; run 2 (`tatqa-wp1b-20261013`) completed the bounded fix. Your job: audit the FINAL artifacts against the binding specification (including revision 1.1) and report verdicts.\n\n## Authorised scope (read-only)\n- `docs/research/WP0_TATQA_ADAPTER_CHECKER_CONTRACT_v1.md` (THE specification)\n- `docs/research/WP0_TATQA_LOOP_A_EXECUTION_PACKAGE_v1.md` (W1-W5, acceptance)\n- `research/tatqa_wp0_2026/wp1/` (implementation_contract.md + .sha256, checker, adapter, fixtures, run_fixtures.py, PREFLIGHT_RECEIPT.json, WP1_RECEIPT.json, PREREG_DRAFT_SKELETON.md)\n- Pinned inputs (read-only): `data/research/tatqa_wp0_2026/` receipts; raw archives headers only if needed.\n\n## Checks\n1. Receipts: `WP1_RECEIPT.json` is valid JSON; declared artifact hashes recompute (`sha256sum`); the four pinned input hashes match; counts 60 items / 182 origins.\n2. The six fixture obligations (contract Sec.3) are each present and not weakened: byte-equal prompts; hidden-gold search; >=5 hand-built recompute fixtures incl. parentheses-negative + thousands separator; the four scale conversions; UNKNOWN/REFUSED classification; E/C token-delta accounting. Quote the code/evidence for each.\n3. Checker: gold is computed before any answer is read; taxonomy classes per contract; spot-check 2-3 fixture recomputations by hand.\n4. Adapter: hidden fields never leak; opaque ids; no arm-dependent truncation; fixed answer format; determinism claim credible.\n5. Preflight: each claim in `PREFLIGHT_RECEIPT.json` is supported by an artifact or a runnable check.\n6. Scope discipline: no model/judge calls, no network, no services; writes confined to wp1 dirs; candidate items were not scored (fixtures are synthetic). Note anything suspicious.\n7. If `python3` execution is denied by your permission gate, replicate statically and say so; Loop D runs the suite natively.\n\n## Output (stdout only)\nPer check: verdict + file:line or hash evidence. Then exactly:\n`LOOP_C_WP1_ITEMS_VERDICT = PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL`\n`LOOP_C_WP1_SPEC_COMPLIANCE_VERDICT = PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL`\n`LOOP_C_WP1_SCOPE_VERDICT = PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL`\n`LOOP_C_WP1_INDEPENDENT_VERDICT = PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL`\nand one closing line naming the single weakest point.\n\n--- dispatch entries ---\nmemory/THREADS.md:7:[10-12] #TH3-WP0-DESIGN-QUALIFICATION-PENDING: [最小科学验证任务卡](../docs/research/thesis_experience_v1_task_card.md) 已完成设计；四臂只识别固定经验包的受限效应，不分离反馈资格的贡献，不证明Memory/SFT或方法创新。下一步仍需只读绑定确切来源/revision/文件/IDs/许可、origin/近重复、参考目标与经验可得性，交导师/owner裁决；`G-RQ=PENDING / G-M=PENDING / METHOD_NOVELTY=NOT_IDENTIFIED`。CONTINUE只支持申请必要性/既有基线比较，未授权WP-1/2。本轮零实验、代码/改稿、模型或GB10访问。\nmemory/STATE.md:11:- WP-0 design is recorded in the existing planned [`task card`](../docs/research/thesis_experience_v1_task_card.md): a bounded given-experience probe, four-arm identification limits, STOP/CONTINUE interpretation and WP-0/WP-1 responsibilities. `DESIGN_COMPLETE / QUALIFICATION_PENDING / EXPERIMENT_NOT_RUN`; exact sources/IDs/rights, real experience and runtime remain unverified. G-RQ/G-M stay PENDING and method novelty NOT_IDENTIFIED. Next entry remains read-only material qualification; no WP-1 implementation or WP-2 run.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
